            <ArticleTitle>Headache competencies in child neurology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.spen.2011.05.011</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a proposal for suggested physician competencies in the diagnosis and treatment of children and adolescent patients with headaches. Headaches are common in childhood and occur in up to 10% of school-aged children and over 20% of female adolescents. Therefore, the appropriate recognition, evaluation, and treatment should be a high priority of training and maintenance of certification programs.</AbstractText>
